[
    {
        "content": "<p>When I run the following code:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">importModules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">loadExts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">CoreM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIO'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``List.isSetoid</span>\n<span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I get <code>false</code>, indicating that <code>List.isSetoid</code> is not an instance (when it is). How do I set up an environment with <code>importModules</code> such that <code>isInstance</code> produces the proper values?</p>",
        "id": 579835388,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773711557
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>perhaps you want to actually import <code>List.isSetoid</code>?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">importModules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">loadExts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Init</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">CoreM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIO'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isInstance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``List.isSetoid</span>\n<span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>since <code>isInstance</code> will report <code>false</code> on nonexistent declarations</p>",
        "id": 579836388,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1773712167
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, that makes sense. I was actually misinterpreting the issue. Consider the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">main</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">importModules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">loadExts</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Mathlib</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">CoreM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toIO'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileName</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fileMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">env</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"here!\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When I use <code>loadExts := true</code>, I need to have the module imported (<code>Mathlib</code> in this case). But when I run <code>lake exe</code> on this file, it doesn't build.</p>",
        "id": 579837837,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773713067
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(it works just fine in an <code>#eval</code> block, or with a less ambitious import like <code>Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic</code>, except I get <code>uncaught exception: unknown module prefix 'Mathlib'</code>)</p>",
        "id": 579837965,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773713165
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It might be worth noting that <code>importModules</code> just attempts to load oleans from where it expects the oleans to be, and unlike <code>lake</code> or the language server, does not ensure that the oleans are present or up to date. I wonder if that could be affecting things?</p>",
        "id": 579841159,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1773715114
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I feel lost as to what I can try. If I don't use loadExts, it runs just fine, except instances are not recognized as isInstance. If I use loadExts, it never makes it to the body, even when Mathlib is imported.</p>",
        "id": 579921428,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773748136
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What does \"doesn't build\" mean? The imports of the surrounding file should be irrelevant</p>",
        "id": 579922171,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1773748387
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, if you don't import Mathlib in the surrounding file, then in builds just fine. If you do import Mathlib, VSCode shows no errors, but <code>lake build</code> reports a large error after reaching Main.lean, ending like so:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">info</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stderr</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"n\">could</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">execute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">external</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">process</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'/</span><span class=\"n\">Users</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">chasenorman</span><span class=\"bp\">/.</span><span class=\"n\">elan</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">toolchains</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">leanprover</span><span class=\"c1\">--lean4---v4.29.0-rc6/bin/clang'</span>\n<span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">external</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'/</span><span class=\"n\">Users</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">chasenorman</span><span class=\"bp\">/.</span><span class=\"n\">elan</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">toolchains</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">leanprover</span><span class=\"c1\">--lean4---v4.29.0-rc6/bin/clang' exited with code 255</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">required</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">targets</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">logged</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failures</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ai</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">exe</span>\n<span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 579922594,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773748517
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And that's without the <code>#eval</code>?</p>",
        "id": 579924574,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1773749054
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is using <code>lake exe</code>, yes.</p>",
        "id": 579924610,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749067
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So build it without importing Mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 579924896,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1773749144
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you run that file, it never makes it past <code>importModules</code></p>",
        "id": 579924967,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749165
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You might just need <code>initSearchPath (← findSysroot)</code></p>",
        "id": 579925033,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1773749181
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have <code>Lean.initSearchPath (← Lean.findSysroot)</code></p>",
        "id": 579925092,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749192
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have added it since the time I put the example above</p>",
        "id": 579925133,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749205
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And <code>supportInterpreter := true</code>?</p>",
        "id": 579925173,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1773749218
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Does that go in the lakefile?</p>",
        "id": 579925297,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749250
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>wow, it works! Is there some documentation I should read about this?</p>",
        "id": 579926008,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749448
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is supposed to be mentioned in an error message. You still haven't been very clear on what the output/build log is without the fix</p>",
        "id": 579927174,
        "sender_full_name": "Sebastian Ullrich",
        "timestamp": 1773749761
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Without the fix, there is no stdout and no stderr. It never makes it past <code>importModules</code>.</p>",
        "id": 579927559,
        "sender_full_name": "Chase Norman",
        "timestamp": 1773749868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I still have no idea what that means. The generated executable hangs? Do you have a stacktrace?</p>",
